{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-x6lg-cutl-dolq-zccb","published":"2026-11-10T02:46:05Z","modified":"2026-11-24T21:46:45.505909892Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-69219"],"summary":"The RabbitMQ Java client library allows Java and JVM-based applications to connect to and interact with RabbitMQ nodes…","details":"The RabbitMQ Java client library allows Java and JVM-based applications to connect to and interact with RabbitMQ nodes. Prior to 5.33.1, src/main/java/com/rabbitmq/client/impl/ValueReader.java uses ValueReader.readBytes to accept a wire-declared contentLength below Integer.MAX_VALUE and allocate a byte array before checking the bytes available in the frame. A malicious AMQP peer can send a LongString or byte-array field with type tag S and a declared length such as 0x7FFFFFFE during the pre-authentication connection.start server-properties table, causing an approximately 2 GB allocation and OutOfMemoryError before readFully consumes data. The resulting memory exhaustion can terminate the JVM and cause denial of service. This issue is fixed in version 5.33.1.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"janusgraph-1.0","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.23","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/janusgraph-1.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"1.0.1-r0"}]}],"versions":["1.0.1-r0","1.0.1-r1","1.0.1-r10","1.0.1-r11","1.0.1-r2","1.0.1-r3","1.0.1-r4","1.0.1-r5","1.0.1-r6","1.0.1-r7","1.0.1-r8","1.0.1-r9"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-x6lg-cutl-dolq-zccb.json"}},{"package":{"name":"janusgraph-1.0","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/janusgraph-1.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"1.0.1-r0"}]}],"versions":["1.0.1-r0","1.0.1-r1","1.0.1-r10","1.0.1-r11","1.0.1-r2","1.0.1-r3","1.0.1-r4","1.0.1-r5","1.0.1-r6","1.0.1-r7","1.0.1-r8","1.0.1-r9"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker